WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
 I am my child, my proud daughter of Richard Ganim.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.000
 It is Trina's honor to accept this recognition on my father's new life.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:17.000
 And I am sorry that due to his ill health, he is not present tonight.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:27.090
 We would like to thank Debbie and Dan Hansen for all the work they did this

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.000
 evening.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.030
 We would like to thank Mr. Pierre Jane for his kind words, his friendship, not

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:40.000
 just tonight, but for many, many years.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.370
 Thank you to my father's Lebanese friends, American friends, church friends,

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:52.000
 city officials friends for being here tonight.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:00.810
 And father and his proud to be Lebanese, but more so he is proud to be an

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.000
 American.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.060
 He loves this country, he has served this country, he believes in three

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.000
 principles.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.950
 You serve your God, you serve your family, you serve your country. He has done

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:16.000
 all three probably.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:25.000
 As Mr. Janey said, he grew up here in America with immigrant parents.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:32.000
 He has been a lifelong member of St. Aaron, Aaron High Catholic Church.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.000
 And he loves his church, he has loved it since the day he was born.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:44.180
 He continues to love it and when he is able to, he attends the church regularly

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:45.000
 there.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.230
 He has done a lesson to all of us, diversity, love everyone, love those who are

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:59.560
 different from you, learn what they are about, learn different faiths, learn

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:02.000
 different cultures.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.740
 Because he really believed that if we learned and we educated ourselves, then

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:11.100
 that is what we would do, we would get along, we would be at peace with one

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.000
 another.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.000
 And that's what he tried to do in his life.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:23.000
 I know as a child growing up, my father loved this country as I said.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.640
 And he served it well, both in the World War II and then coming home and

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:30.000
 serving the city of Seven Hills.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.000
 He loved politics. He thrived on it.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:45.160
 And along with minor George, he started cameo, an organization that to this day

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:47.000
 still thrives.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:53.790
 So I would like to congratulate those who are also getting inducted along with

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.000
 my father.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.440
 He is humbled to be included in such a district, the distinguished class, and I

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:04.000
 once again regret that he is unable to attend tonight.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.240
 [APPLAUSE]

